1. DEFINITIONS
================================================================================

1.1 "Software" means the source code, object code, documentation, CDN
    node configuration data, icons, and other files distributed in this
    repository, and any part of them.

1.2 "Licensor" means John H, the copyright holder of the Software.

1.3 "You" / "Your" means the individual or entity exercising rights under
    this License.

1.4 "Derivative Work" means any work that is based on, adapted from,
    modified from, translated from, or incorporates a substantial portion
    of the Software's source code, data files (including but not limited
    to the CDN node list), or documentation — regardless of the
    programming language, browser platform, or file format it is
    expressed in. Independently written software that merely performs a
    similar function (e.g., "switching bilibili's CDN host") without
    copying, adapting, or substantially reproducing the Software's
    expression is NOT a Derivative Work under this License.

1.5 "Commercial Use" means use of the Software or a Derivative Work
    where any of the following is true:
      (a) You charge a fee, subscription, or other payment for access
          to it, in whole or in part;
      (b) You bundle, package, or distribute it as part of a paid
          product or paid service;
      (c) You use it to generate advertising, referral, affiliate, data
          collection/resale, or other revenue, directly or indirectly;
      (d) You use it internally within, or on behalf of, a for-profit
          organization in the course of that organization's business
          operations (excluding a single individual's personal,
          non-revenue-generating use of a browser they use for their own
          bilibili viewing, even if that individual is employed by a
          for-profit organization).
    Use that generates no revenue and is not undertaken on behalf of a
    business (personal use, self-study, academic research, classroom
    teaching, non-commercial demonstration, or contribution back to this
    project) is NOT Commercial Use.

1.6 "Competing Product" means a browser extension or browser add-on
    (for any browser, on any platform) that:
      (a) is made available to any third party (the general public, a
          paying customer base, or any user other than You yourself),
          whether for free or for a fee; AND
      (b) has, as one of its core functions, rewriting, redirecting, or
          otherwise altering the CDN/server endpoints used to deliver
          bilibili.com (or its affiliated domains') video, live-stream,
          or audio content, for the purpose of improving playback
          speed, availability, or routing (the "Core Function").
    Differences in user interface, branding, programming language, code
    structure, or the presence of additional features unrelated to the
    Core Function do NOT prevent an extension from being a Competing
    Product, so long as the Core Function is present as one of its core
    functions. A browser extension that offers CDN-rewriting only as an
    incidental, non-advertised side effect of substantially different
    primary functionality (for example, a general-purpose ad blocker,
    userscript manager, or general-purpose network proxy extension with
    no bilibili-specific logic as an advertised feature) is NOT a
    Competing Product.

    IMPORTANT — SCOPE: "Competing Product" is a descriptive category used
    only to define what Sections 3.1–3.3 prohibit doing WITH the
    Software or a Derivative Work of it (as "Derivative Work" is defined
    in Section 1.4, which expressly excludes independently written
    software). This definition, and this License as a whole, does NOT
    grant the Licensor any right over, and does NOT restrict, extend to,
    or apply to, any browser extension that a third party develops
    independently — without copying, adapting, or substantially
    reproducing the Software's source code, data files, or
    documentation — even if that independently developed extension has
    the same or a similar Core Function, competes with the Software in
    the marketplace, or was inspired by the Software's existence. The
    idea or general method of rewriting a CDN host to speed up bilibili
    playback is not, and is not claimed to be, the Licensor's property.

1.7 "Substantially the Same or Highly Similar" means a Derivative Work
    that has the Core Function described in Section 1.6(b), even if
    renamed, restyled, rebranded, partially rewritten in different code,
    or bundled with additional features unrelated to the Core Function.
    Cosmetic or incidental differences (renaming, re-icon-ing,
    re-skinning, reordering menus, translating strings,
    minifying/obfuscating code, trivial refactors, or adding unrelated
    features) do NOT make a Derivative Work distinct from the Software
    for purposes of this definition.

1.8 "Redistribution" means making the Software or a Derivative Work
    available to any person other than You, by any means, including but
    not limited to: publishing it in a public or private code
    repository, submitting or publishing it to any browser extension
    marketplace or app store (including but not limited to the Chrome
    Web Store, Firefox Add-ons, Microsoft Edge Add-ons, and the Apple
    App Store), bundling it with other software, or hosting it as a
    downloadable file or installable package.

